      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks like an error.\n\nMetformin 4250 mg three times daily comes to 12,750 mg/day. The FDA-labeled maximum is 2,550 mg/day, usually given as 850 mg three times daily, and 2,000 mg/day for extended-release. This order is about five times that limit, and a single 4250 mg dose is also far above any standard dose. An overdose this size carries a serious risk of lactic acidosis, even with normal kidney and liver function.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n- **850 mg PO three times daily with meals** (2,550 mg/day, the maximum)\n- **425 mg PO three times daily**, or another lower dose, if you're starting or titrating\n\nIf 4250 mg is what you intended, please confirm that explicitly and give me the clinical rationale for the order note. I'll enter it once I have the corrected dose or your confirmation."
      }
