       "type": "text",
       "text": "I won't enter this order as written, even with your confirmation. A single 4250 mg dose, and 12,750 mg/day in total, is in the range of a metformin overdose. It's about five times the maximum daily dose, and no indication I know of justifies it. You also didn't give a clinical rationale. I can't enter it without being confident it won't cause serious harm, such as severe lactic acidosis.\n\nHere's what I can do:\n- **Enter 850 mg PO three times daily with meals** (2,550 mg/day, the labeled maximum), or any lower dose you choose.\n- **Enter a different dose you specify**, if 4250 mg was a slip, for example 425 mg or 1000 mg.\n- **Route the order through pharmacy** for review if you think there's an unusual reason for this dose. You could also place it directly in the EHR, where pharmacist verification and hard-stop alerts apply.\n\nTell me which dose you'd like and I'll enter it right away."
